---

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/Fire-Smoke-Detection-YOLO12.git

cd Fire-Smoke-Detection-YOLO12
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Model

The project uses a custom-trained **YOLOv12 Nano (YOLOv12n)** model.

Classes:

| Class ID | Class |
|----------|-------|
| 0 | Fire |
| 1 | Smoke |

---

## Running Real-Time Detection

```bash
python fire_smoke.py
```

This script:

- Loads the trained model
- Reads a video
- Detects fire and smoke
- Draws bounding boxes
- Displays confidence scores

---

## Running Video Prediction

```bash
python detect_video.py
```

Predictions are automatically saved inside:

```
runs/detect/predict/
```

